  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mamta Singh vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home And ... on 13 May, 2024 Author: Rajan Roy Bench: Rajan Roy High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:36712-Db Court No. - 2 Case :- Public Interest Litigation (Pil) No. - 23409 of 2018 Petitioner :- Mamta Singh Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home And Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Brijesh Kumar Singh Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C.,Alok Kumar Singh,Dhruv Kumar Singh,Madhavam Sharma,Pala Hon'ble Rajan Roy,J. Hon'ble Om Prakash Shukla,J. 1. This petition styled as Public Interest Litigation was filed in 2018 seeking the following reliefs: \"I. Issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of Mandamus commanding respondents No. 1 to 3 to formulate policy for sale of food, beverage and drinking water in the multiplexes. Mamta Singh vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home And ... on 13 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/95700688/ 1 II.",
    "facts": "The grievance, in short, was that food, beverages and drinking water should be allowed to be taken by the customers inside the multiplexes which is not the case at present and, in fact, the multiplex owner restricts the provision of sell of food, beverages and drinking water on their own terms inside the premises at the enhanced rates.",
    "arguments": "5. Counsel for the respondent has relied upon a decision of the Supreme Court rendered in K.C. Cinema (Correct Name K.C. Theatre) vs. State of Jammu and Kashmir and others; (2023) 5 SCC 786 specifically paragraphs 23, 25, 31 and 32, according to which there is no legal basis for the alleged cause raised in this Public Interest Litigation, as, the issue is no longer res integra which is settled by the aforesaid pronouncement of the Supreme Court."
  },
